{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/993520-syndicate-ve-relationship","id":993520,"title":"Syndicate-VE relationship?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-26T08:54:18-07:00","id":993520,"title":"Syndicate-VE relationship?","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They keep submitting requests for weapons and military training in order to counter something they call \u201cThreat Null,\u201d<br /> but don\u2019t shed much light on. Honestly, one of the few places where we see eye to eye with NWO is our distrust of the Void Engineers, but you know what they say: keep your enemies close. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In this case, that means funding them enough to make them feel in the family, while keeping them on as much of a leash as possible. De-prioritizing space exploration in the West has helped to lessen their hold on government and public alike (though, not without resentment), and sends a clear message that they need to cover their bottom line or else. </div> </div> </div>Firstly, why VE needs to request weapons and training to the Syndics in any way? They already have more than enough weapon foundries, arsenals and training facilities. Furthermore, VE's weapons and training vastly outclass the Syndicate counterparts...and for that matter, anything other Conventions could hope to provide.<br /> <br /> Secondly, text says as if Syndicate played an active part of de-prioritization of space exploration in the West. But I find that is implausible - if there is a Convention possess enough political power and will(and motivation) to wield it, that would be NWO, not Syndicate. That sort of thing is NWO's job, not the Syndics, after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","user":"Numinous","date":". 10-26-2016, 02:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","name":"Numinous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T09:23:53-07:00","id":993532,"title":"","content":"Firstly, who do you think pays for all these weapons, ammunition, maintenance, training, recruiting, facilities, staff, etc.? Without the funding of the Syndicate, the VE's would barely have the resources to build a single rocket let alone the fleet they require for Space Exploration, and gauntlet patrol.<br /> <br /> Secondly, While NWO can control the world from the shadows with their influence in universities, governments, information bureaus, and all kinds of surveillance from CCTV to internet security; it's the Syndicate that run the world in the bright of day. They are the reason Capitalism dominates the western landscape. Just to give you an idea of of the reach this gives them, think about everything you have, every book, every bit of tech, every piece of food. Does it have a brand name on it? The chances are the Technocracy can control it.<br /> They are the large corporations that get votes all to themselves, the news agents and media outlets which spin journalism to create a message the masses want to hear, they fund movies, tv shows, all kinds of stories designed to inspire people towards the Technocratic paradigm, and sell off the Tradition's arts and tools as simple magic shows with costumes and props.<br /> <br /> While the NWO can manipulate the leaders of the west into their way of thinking directly, the Syndicate can shift the opinion of the masses, making certain things less or more popular simply by increasing availability, or drawing attention to them in a negative way, and thus manipulate the leaders of the western world indirectly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 10-26-2016, 02:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T09:54:51-07:00","id":993547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/993520-syndicate-ve-relationship?p=993532#post993532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Firstly, who do you think pays for all these weapons, ammunition, maintenance, training, recruiting, facilities, staff, etc.? Without the funding of the Syndicate, the VE's would barely have the resources to build a single rocket let alone the fleet they require for Space Exploration, and gauntlet patrol.<br /> <br /> Secondly, While NWO can control the world from the shadows with their influence in universities, governments, information bureaus, and all kinds of surveillance from CCTV to internet security; it's the Syndicate that run the world in the bright of day. They are the reason Capitalism dominates the western landscape. Just to give you an idea of of the reach this gives them, think about everything you have, every book, every bit of tech, every piece of food. Does it have a brand name on it? The chances are the Technocracy can control it.<br /> They are the large corporations that get votes all to themselves, the new agents and media outlets which spin journalism to create a message the masses want to hear, they fund movies, tv shows, all kinds of stories designed to inspire people towards the Technocratic paradigm, and sell off the Tradition's arts and tools as simple magic shows with costumes and props.<br /> <br /> While the NWO can manipulate the leaders of the west into their way of thinking directly, the Syndicate can shift the opinion of the masses, making certain things less or more popular simply by increasing availability, or drawing attention to them in a negative way, and thus manipulate the leaders of the western world indirectly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Firstly, Void Engineers could build their own things in space. They have always done that. They have numerous shipyards, bases, labs, facilities, nodes, habitats, and hell, even <i>colonies </i>in the Void. And in any case, VE outright requests &quot;weapons and military training&quot;, not funding(building materials, Primal Energy, et cetra.)<br /> <br /> Secondly, I completely agree with you. Thank you for great answer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","user":"Numinous","date":". 10-26-2016, 02:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","name":"Numinous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T11:28:52-07:00","id":993605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/993520-syndicate-ve-relationship?p=993547#post993547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Firstly, Void Engineers could build their own things in space. They have always done that. They have numerous shipyards, bases, labs, facilities, nodes, habitats, and hell, even <i>colonies </i>in the Void. And in any case, VE outright requests &quot;weapons and military training&quot;, not funding(building materials, Primal Energy, et cetra.)</div> </div> </div> </div>They might have been able to do this, if the Dimensional Anomaly hadn't come along and wrecked up almost all of their constructs, killed of thousands of their best scientists, and made even entering space a nontrivial matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T12:51:46-07:00","id":993646,"title":"","content":"The weapons and military training are because the VE are going on a war footing. Every rear-echelon guy gets a rifle and a day on the range, then they get on the transport. They don't need more Constructs, they need firepower.<br /> <br /> It makes sense that the Syndicate deprioritized space exploration in the West, because most of the reason was we couldn't afford it. NASA's budget kept getting slashed. You don't have to be in the White House to make that happen - all you have to do is make everything else the government spends money on <i>more expensive</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7356-haldir2012","name":"haldir2012","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T13:44:18-07:00","id":993672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haldir2012</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/993520-syndicate-ve-relationship?p=993646#post993646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The weapons and military training are because the VE are going on a war footing. Every rear-echelon guy gets a rifle and a day on the range, then they get on the transport. They don't need more Constructs, they need firepower.<br /> <br /> It makes sense that the Syndicate deprioritized space exploration in the West, because most of the reason was we couldn't afford it. NASA's budget kept getting slashed. You don't have to be in the White House to make that happen - all you have to do is make everything else the government spends money on <i>more expensive</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. So basically the Syndicate provides mass-produced Extraordinary Devises and fresh meat for the grinder to the VE?<br /> <br /> 2. Oh, that makes sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","name":"Numinous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T16:12:09-07:00","id":993762,"title":"","content":"For every space ship the VEs are building themselves, it's eating up the time of Enlightened and Extraordinary Personnel that the VE can't spare. They need every person they have to protect earth from the forces of multiple dimensional angles of attack and from everything in space.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T08:11:29-07:00","id":994593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TidyGamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/993520-syndicate-ve-relationship?p=993762#post993762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For every space ship the VEs are building themselves, it's eating up the time of Enlightened and Extraordinary Personnel that the VE can't spare. They need every person they have to protect earth from the forces of multiple dimensional angles of attack and from everything in space.</div> </div> </div> </div>What do you mean is...the Syndicate is providing weapons and training and personnel to the Earthside VEs?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","name":"Numinous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T08:50:18-07:00","id":994615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/993520-syndicate-ve-relationship?p=994593#post994593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you mean is...the Syndicate is providing weapons and training and personnel to the Earthside VEs?</div> </div> </div> </div>Who else pays for the assembly line?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T09:58:39-07:00","id":994643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/993520-syndicate-ve-relationship?p=994593#post994593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you mean is...the Syndicate is providing weapons and training and personnel to the Earthside VEs?</div> </div> </div> </div>It provides funding to support those things, yes. I think the VE book talks about there being one remaining operational underwater spaceship manufacturing plant and that sort of thing isn't cheap to keep operational. The Syndicate keeps it supplied with materials (which are often supplied by Iteration X and the Progenitors in exchange for their own funding) and personnel (who are either supplied in house by the VE or are recruited through the NWO or Syndicate) and it keeps those movements <i>secret from the world at large</i>. You can't use Wormhole generators to move that stuff every step of the way, sometimes you have to use 'legitimate' shipping interests crewed by extraordinary personnel (which are just sleepers who have gone through stage 7 processing).<br /> <br /> The VE isn't self sufficient, if it was forced to dedicate people to staffing Enlightened Hydroponic Farms enough to feed everyone on it's payroll, it would loose huge chunks of medical personnel needed on the front lines. If it was forced to dedicate people to fabricating the materials it needs to build and maintain all it's equipment in space, then lots of places that need those engineers in the field would suffer because of it. They have to re-proccess everyone who is likely to encounter Threat Null, if they had to devote the personnel needed for that to processing everyone then both aspects would grind to a halt.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T10:01:24-07:00","id":994645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/993520-syndicate-ve-relationship?p=994615#post994615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Who else pays for the assembly line?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;pays?&quot; No, they are Enlightened. They don't need money to produce weapon - at least in conventional sense. What they need is Primal Energy and rare materials. And it seems VEs are requesting assembly-line hypertech anyway, instead of money and other resources need to run that line.<br /> <br /> And like I said, VEs are still manufacturing and supplying their own weapons - it is curious why they demand the Syndicate to procure Enlightened weapons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","name":"Numinous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T10:04:02-07:00","id":994646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TidyGamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/993520-syndicate-ve-relationship?p=994643#post994643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It provides funding to support those things, yes. I think the VE book talks about there being one remaining operational underwater spaceship manufacturing plant and that sort of thing isn't cheap to keep operational. The Syndicate keeps it supplied with materials (which are often supplied by Iteration X and the Progenitors in exchange for their own funding) and personnel (who are either supplied in house by the VE or are recruited through the NWO or Syndicate) and it keeps those movements <i>secret from the world at large</i>. You can't use Wormhole generators to move that stuff every step of the way, sometimes you have to use 'legitimate' shipping interests crewed by extraordinary personnel (which are just sleepers who have gone through stage 7 processing).<br /> <br /> The VE isn't self sufficient, if it was forced to dedicate people to staffing Enlightened Hydroponic Farms enough to feed everyone on it's payroll, it would loose huge chunks of medical personnel needed on the front lines. If it was forced to dedicate people to fabricating the materials it needs to build and maintain all it's equipment in space, then lots of places that need those engineers in the field would suffer because of it. They have to re-proccess everyone who is likely to encounter Threat Null, if they had to devote the personnel needed for that to processing everyone then both aspects would grind to a halt.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, that makes <i>a lot of</i> sense. Thank you so much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","name":"Numinous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T10:44:07-07:00","id":994664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/993520-syndicate-ve-relationship?p=994645#post994645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;pays?&quot; No, they are Enlightened. They don't need money to produce weapon - at least in conventional sense. What they need is Primal Energy and rare materials. And it seems VEs are requesting assembly-line hypertech anyway, instead of money and other resources need to run that line.<br /> <br /> And like I said, VEs are still manufacturing and supplying their own weapons - it is curious why they demand the Syndicate to procure Enlightened weapons.</div> </div> </div> </div>You still need to pay for those resources. The metal to come out of the ground, to be refined and workable, the machines needed to shape the metal into the tools and parts they need... It all costs. Then there's the technicians who build this stuff, they all have salaries to pay.<br /> Primal Energy itself costs a heck of a lot to extract, transport, store, protect, and ensure it doesn't lose potency over time.<br /> <br /> It all costs, whether it's being outsourced or done in house with imported materials. It all costs though, and it's the business enterprises forged by the Syndicate which makes the industries all of this assembly relies on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T10:46:20-07:00","id":994667,"title":"","content":"The greatest strength of the Union is that the Conventions work together. Everyone supplies things that the other Conventions require, so they can afford to specialize. NWO provides control, Syndicate provides infrastructure, Void Engineers provide safety, Progenitors provides medical and Iteration X provides materials. The problem with providing &quot;safety&quot; is that it's invisible and intangible unless there's a failure in supplying it. The Syndicate KNOWS that what the VE is doing is vital, but the VE has to keep secrets and that makes it difficult to understand the scope of threats that the VE holds back.<br /> <br /> If you had a buddy who would vanish for months at a time to wrestle tigers that threaten you with minimal contact and who blew you off with vague allusions to things that they wouldn't fully explain, only to come knocking with some new scars, a hollow look in their eyes (proving that they are indeed wrestling tigers) and wanting to restock his cooler and recharge his phone, would you just be a-okay with letting them do so (considering that there's four other groups who also want to use the same things they want and are providing more concrete reasons for letting them have the stuff)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T03:36:49-07:00","id":995141,"title":"","content":"I kinda assumed from the way the Syndicate book is written that when they're talking about money they're to a large degree talking about primal energy, which the Syndicate conceptualises with primal value.<br /> <br /> Though, I admit that may be me reading more into it than was intended.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T04:10:08-07:00","id":995149,"title":"","content":"No, it's straight currency too. The Void Engineers can't devote huge amounts of manpower towards operating their own mines, foundries, and fields. Even if we assume they do that in the Umbra, it's a pain in the ass to transport raw materials from said Umbra to the material plane, to be processed. And there's stuff on this side of the Gauntlet that the VEs need those materials for. It's a whole hell of a lot easier - and easier to hide - if they just have the Syndicate handle the mind-numbing economic work of obtaining raw materials, transporting them where they're needed, and hiding all of it within shell companies and the like.<br /> <br /> Just relying on Primal Energy to materialize everything they need isn't practical. Not on the scales the Void Engineers need them on. They build space stations and starships, for crying out loud. That stuff is complicated and resource intensive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T09:53:29-07:00","id":995244,"title":"","content":"You don't need Primal Energy to materialize anything. You just need Prime and Matter. Prime isn't a restricted Sphere. Tons of VE's are going to have it. In fact, they can probably make pretty much everything they want with just Matter. They don't need dick from the Syndicate or the world to just make any sort of mundane stuff. They have infinite supplies of normal materials and normal energy and normal foods. <br /> <br /> What they don't have is Quintessence and, unless you are tossing EDE's into a &quot;Gnosis to Quintessence&quot; converter or use your fellow VE's as batteries in a Matrix-like fashion, it's pretty damn hard to get. Also, as pointed out, when fighting the good fight is pretty much all you're doing, you can't afford to have your best Device builders sitting there churning out Devices. You need them out there on the ships acting like Scotty, doing wild upgrades and repair work on the fly in the field. (And that was probably what most of them were supposed to be doing back in the good old exploration days as well.). Last, but not least, they REALLY need some way to keep Void Adaptation from setting in. (Especially now they've seen where that all ends in the form of Threat Null.)<br /> <br /> That's what the Syndicate is doing. It isn't supplying them with the normal stuff. (In the Technocratic paradigm, they've made getting resources into space prohibitively costly in any case.) The economy of Earth is effectively a Quintessence farming operation through use of Primal Utility. Though the VE's objectives aren't the only recipient of that (or even the one with the largest market share), that's what the Syndicate is doing. Of course, that Quintessence has to take some form and it's not all in charged-up Matricies. A lot of it is in the form of complete Devices (with/through Iteration X). It's also in what might look like raw materials, but are actually very much more than that. (Create a factory that makes parts that are used in the manufacture of Voidships that is a Primal Venture. Use Primal Utility to funnel the Quintessence generated into the parts that are being made... they aren't Devices, more like super-dedicated Tass. Shoot the parts into space They are definitely worth it.) In fact, those Matricies are being produced the same way... the Quintessence filled &quot;reactor cores&quot; or whatever are the parts in question.<br /> <br /> It's also why the other Conventions are pretty important as well. Either the NWO (&quot;political officers&quot;), Progenitors (those archetypal medical officers) or both are probably helping out with making sure that VE personnel are able to rotate out so Void Adaptation doesn't come into play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T18:12:40-07:00","id":995461,"title":"","content":"Yeah, but there are not a lot of Void Engineers. If we go by the canon populations, there Mages are 1:100,000. Asia possesses its own Mages (even the Five Elemental Dragon are different than the Technocracy), so we will remove half of the global population, leaving 35,000 Mages. 20% of them are probably Technocrats, and 20% of them are probably Void Engineers, leaving 1,400 Mages. 1,400 Mages is not that many to defend the Earth from the Outer Dark. .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T10:29:28-07:00","id":995701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/993520-syndicate-ve-relationship?p=995461#post995461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, but there are not a lot of Void Engineers. If we go by the canon populations, there Mages are 1:100,000. Asia possesses its own Mages (even the Five Elemental Dragon are different than the Technocracy), so we will remove half of the global population, leaving 35,000 Mages. 20% of them are probably Technocrats, and 20% of them are probably Void Engineers, leaving 1,400 Mages. 1,400 Mages is not that many to defend the Earth from the Outer Dark. .</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering China's taikonauts are considered important to and even the new major source of (or at least A major source of) VE's according to the new VE book, it's probably out of line to take out all of Asia. Japan has always had an active interest and participation in space programs. The Central Asian Republics have been the physical location of almost all of the USSR/Russian space program. Also, India is getting very involved in space exploration and was never considered under the influence of the Elemental Dragons. (Oh, and since the Elemental Dragons is part of that Asian fetish phase of White Wolf and might not even be much of a thing anymore.<br /> <br /> So, add all those folks back in. Plus, as you are very very fond of Extraordinary Citizens and there are definitely more than a few of them explicitly associated with the VEs out in Conventional Space, you've got all of them holding down the various Technical Specialty positions their specific super-science prowess sets them up for, plus some mentions of appropriately prepped and decked out Sympathizers as well. Not to mention, that there are different settings for &quot;VE Paranoia&quot; leading to the exclusion of relevant personnel from other Conventions when and where appropriate. If you don't set them at &quot;Absolutely NO non-VE personnel in Space&quot; (which, TBH, is the default for a Threat Null game.. even though that would seem to tip the VE's hidden hand 100% that they are hiding SOMETHING from everyone else.... and that's just plain unmutual of them that would warrant some serious investigation), then there might even be some members of other Conventions out there as well (particularly It-X, who are even explicitly marked out as being out there in the starting fiction of the new VE book, which is definitely an internal contradiction to the overall Threat Null stance). <br /> <br /> On the other hand. the VE's have a lot of little niches to fill, many of them dealing with more terrestrial concerns. So you do need to carve out a chunk of their total number space-faring personnel to go spelunking, Ghostbuster-ing, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T12:53:41-07:00","id":995759,"title":"","content":"I hardly consider it a fetish to try to include the 50% of humanity previously ignored in the cWoD, even if it was not a very good representation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T13:56:31-07:00","id":995795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/993520-syndicate-ve-relationship?p=995759#post995759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hardly consider it a fetish to try to include the 50% of humanity previously ignored in the cWoD, even if it was not a very good representation.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is NOT what they did. At all. Unless you consider more than an insignificant amount of outright cultural appropriation without any real knowledge of what they were taking and a definite lack of taste all over the place through a lens of anime fanboy adulation &quot;including 50% of humanity&quot;. (Which isn't really correct either... India has never really been treated with any agree of actual attention and that's a significant chunk of the population of Asia and humanity overall). Not that everything they did was outright horrible, but there are reasons that there are things that have been outright rejected (Wu Keng, anyone?) by a game system that rejects NOTHING from its past, no matter how inconvenient or problematic it makes in moving things forwards, and others that are so heavily freighted with stereotypes that many have a hate-hate relationship with them. (There are many out there who are un-fans of KoE and, for many different parts of it, they aren't even vaguely wrong).<br /> <br /> And yes, The Elemental Dragons are definitely a part of that, for good or ill. If it's Asian it <i><b>has </b></i>to be <i><b>different</b></i>.... That's.... not good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T15:34:28-07:00","id":995829,"title":"","content":"Asia is different than the USA or Europe. If you claim otherwise, you are negating the importance of their culture, history, religion, etc. There is no real reason for Asians (or Africans for that matter) to not have different perspectives or objectives than Americans or Europeans. By saying otherwise, you ignore the suffering caused by centuries of American and European imperialism that was devoted to the idea of negating the autonomy of Asians and Africans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T16:16:33-07:00","id":995852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/993520-syndicate-ve-relationship?p=995795#post995795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yes, The Elemental Dragons are definitely a part of that, for good or ill. If it's Asian it <i><b>has </b></i>to be <i><b>different</b></i>.... That's.... not good.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whether it's good or not, East Asian philosophies regarding a lot of things Westerners take for granted as &quot;normal&quot; is different. That's just how culture works.<br /> Heck, there are many differences between countries as culturally similar as the USA and the UK.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T09:50:58-07:00","id":996121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/993520-syndicate-ve-relationship?p=995829#post995829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Asia is different than the USA or Europe. If you claim otherwise, you are negating the importance of their culture, history, religion, etc. There is no real reason for Asians (or Africans for that matter) to not have different perspectives or objectives than Americans or Europeans. By saying otherwise, you ignore the suffering caused by centuries of American and European imperialism that was devoted to the idea of negating the autonomy of Asians and Africans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Canada is different from the United States. The UK is different from Canada and the US. Europe is different from the UK. The constituent parts of Europe are different from each other. Europe is very different than Africa. Super-Saharan Africa is different from Sub-Saharan Africa. East Africa is different from West Africa. Somalia is different from Tanzania. The Hadza are different from the rest of the Tanzanians. All of East African is different from the state of South Africa (which includes several nations, since nation = ethnic group + land).<br /> <br /> Mexico is different from the United States. Mexico is different from the other countries of Central America. Central America is different from South America. The different nations of South America are different from one another....<br /> <br /> And so on.<br /> <br /> Why is Asia so special and so different? So special as to have separate sourcebooks (at LEAST 1, sometimes more) in 4 different game lines and have it's own complete spin-off line from another? If you are going to shoehorn werewolves into Asian culture despite without any respect whatsoever as to how werewolves fit or don't fit into Asian culture? Why not shoehorn in everything else and make your global game lines actually global? Asia is definitely picked out as different and lavished with time care and attention. Particularly in areas that are &quot;bright and shiny&quot; to Westerners. Without much sensitivity to the broad variety of actual cultures involved. China has 56 separate identified ethnicities within it's borders. That's identified by the Han majority. Treatment of the others in game products is sparse to non-existent. We were given the Wu Keng but completely ignored, say, the Mosuo who have very interesting and unique takes on spiritualism, etc.? (Guess they're just Dreamspeakers.... but, clearly, the Syndicate is displaced by the Zaibatsu and Asia's economy is separated from that of the world at large. Take that Hang Seng!) And that's not to mention the treatment that is given to, say, Viet Nam or Indonesia. (How about Papua New Guinea? ANYTHING? Nope... Not even in an Australian book as an aside in box as far as I can suss out.)<br /> <br /> Africa is pretty much an afterthought. What minor nods to Africa came much much later and aren't even a handful of books, a few chapters here and there and some off-hand mentions. It's better than, say, what almost all of South America ended up with, or Central or North Asia, or the Indian subcontinent, or really, to a degree, the Near &amp; Middle East, but only just.<br /> <br /> If your standard for inclusion is effectively a mass of cultural appropriation (which is a BAD thing) and material cherry-picked based on it's perceived current (to that time) &quot;coolness&quot;, then sure they did a bang-up job on China and some other places that people have heard of. And they poked at African like the broccoli on your plate you'd rather not eat. In fact, it has been said (again and again) that there are definite and definable ways in which the treatment of Asia as presented <i><b>perpetuates </b></i>the stereotypes created during imperialism, not in any way negating &quot;centuries of suffering&quot; and &quot;negating the autonomy&quot; of the region in question. And not just here and there, as thick veins throughout.<br /> <br /> The question is not whether not this is the case. It is. That's a professional opinion as a professor of anthropology and archaeology and it's definitely one that has expressed by many many others, including game designers in various ways here and there over the years. The question is how much can be used as is, salvaged vs. how much should be discarded, paved over, forgotten, tweaked, etc. It's not an issue of lumping, it's chosing when and how you lump. There's no way that every culture, ethnicity, nation can be included. They can't. There isn't a Ju/'hoansi sourcebook and there never should be. Particularly not one for Vampire, another for Werewolf, and still more for Wraith, Changeling and Mage. It's breaking the world down into chunks and managing it in a way that is doable in the game and is more reasonable and aware of what is actually out there in places where the situation is overall more different from the modern Western &quot;baseline&quot; from which the game can (and should, and, in fact, must) operate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T10:29:36-07:00","id":996137,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1062_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1062\" data-vbnamecard=\"1062\">Ajax</a> I was going to write a long thing about how I disagreed because I considered fear of Cultural Appropriation to be rather harmful towards inclusivity and creates a form of cultural segregation, which is a terrible thing for anyone. But the more I read over your post, the more I realised that wasn't actually what you were talking about.<br /> <br /> I agree with what you're saying. If someone is going to explore a particular culture in their work, they have a duty to do it with respect and accuracy, rather than just gut it for the &quot;cool&quot; parts and sell it under the illusion of being diverse.<br /> <br /> That being said, the fact that they focused their world outside of Europe and the USA was a good thing. Sure it was done with the &quot;Oh yeah! Asia!&quot; sentiment, but it opened the door to thinking of these games outside of their presented context.<br /> It might have been a flawed start, but it was a start none the less, and a step towards improvement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 10-31-2016, 01:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T11:28:08-07:00","id":996163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/993520-syndicate-ve-relationship?p=996137#post996137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1062_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1062\" data-vbnamecard=\"1062\">Ajax</a> I was going to write a long thing about how I disagreed because I considered fear of Cultural Appropriation to be rather harmful towards inclusivity and creates a form of cultural segregation, which is a terrible thing for anyone. But the more I read over your post, the more I realised that wasn't actually what you were talking about.<br /> <br /> I agree with what you're saying. If someone is going to explore a particular culture in their work, they have a duty to do it with respect and accuracy, rather than just gut it for the &quot;cool&quot; parts and sell it under the illusion of being diverse.<br /> <br /> That being said, the fact that they focused their world outside of Europe and the USA was a good thing. Sure it was done with the &quot;Oh yeah! Asia!&quot; sentiment, but it opened the door to thinking of these games outside of their presented context.<br /> It might have been a flawed start, but it was a start none the less, and a step towards improvement.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do not disagree with you on the idea of the sentiment to reach for the unknown. I don't know if you were playing White Wolf games at the time, but it definitely seemed like a step in the right direction. There is definitely some defenses that can be raised concerning the original attempts, particularly the difficulty of getting information in a pre-searchable internet environment. <br /> <br /> However, those times have passed and it's time to put away the things that, in retrospect, weren't really good ideas. There are definitely some ideas that need to be shelved next to the Gypsies book, where Changeling stated that autism was dangerously Banal to changelings, etc. We've seen some good stabs at it with the lack of Wu Keng in M20 and there is no doubt that a new Akashayana splat book would almost certainly be an improvement over either Akashic Brotherhood book, etc. <br /> <br /> But I would REALLY like to see something more definitive and less tentative about India...<br /> <br /> Anyways....sorry about the digressions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T18:45:05-07:00","id":996388,"title":"","content":"I have been playing WoD since 1992, and I remember everything. Yes, we have become more sensitive people, but we are talking about supernatural creatures in a dark reflection of the world. Why should the supernatural creatures of Asia not be different than the supernatural creatures of Europe? Why should everything have to be about supporting the narrative of the Western imperialism?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T00:13:56-07:00","id":996478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They\u2019re trying to sell us a future; it\u2019s not hard to see the Enlightened puppet strings around the birth of commercial space flight. Granted, they don\u2019t get what we\u2019re trying to<br /> do, so they\u2019re fucking it up a bit by seeing everything in their paradigm of \u201cprofits\u201d rather than of exploration. But you gotta give credit where it\u2019s due \u2014 they aren\u2019t throwing around the antagonism toward us as NWO does. </div> </div> </div>...and now the Syndicate is creating entities like Space X and Orbital Sciences Corporation. Yesterday's enemy, today's friend.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","name":"Numinous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T10:57:03-07:00","id":997242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/993520-syndicate-ve-relationship?p=996388#post996388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have been playing WoD since 1992, and I remember everything. Yes, we have become more sensitive people, but we are talking about supernatural creatures in a dark reflection of the world. Why should the supernatural creatures of Asia not be different than the supernatural creatures of Europe? Why should everything have to be about supporting the narrative of the Western imperialism?</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps, because, as I said, the narrative you are supporting is intrinsically tied to the imperialism you decry? <br /> <br /> If your supernatural creatures in a dark world largely conform to the Western stereotypes (and they largely do), then you are not being inclusive by making them different, you are reemphasizing the negative stereotypes created by and maintained by imperialism. We did not get a holistic examination of the Asian supernatural, we got a Western fanboy interpretation of the Asian supernatural at a time when &quot;Asian&quot; (for certain values of Asian which are very non-inclusive) was the &quot;cool&quot; thing. Which is, once again, why we have &quot;everything Asian is different, even when it's the same (vide Hengeyokai)&quot;, when, by your logic, everything, everywhere that's not primarily modern Western culture should be just as different.<br /> <br /> That's not to say there aren't some matters that are well-handled, but the overall framework is creaky with the same ideas you seem to think aren't there. You can't build something that isn't stereotypical and a part of the continuum of Western imperialism if you are pedaling long-standing stereotypes through the lens of a then-current stereotype, and, in the process, by exclusion also reinforcing many of the same and many more additional stereotypes by choosing to pick out this one area to the exclusion of all others, which by omission you are consigning to being not as special, e.g. they DON'T have supernatural dimensions determined by their intrinsic cultures. There is just &quot;the East&quot; (meaning almost entirely the area regarded as being with the sphere of cultural influence of China, or, to be more precise the area over which China maintains that it exerts cultural hegemony) and &quot;the West&quot; (literally EVERYWHERE else). <br /> <br /> Which doesn't help with the central issue in the thread at all. If you want Elemental Dragons to be exclusive to and excluding all things Technocratic and Western, then you are faced with a difficulty presented by several factors: The global nature of the Union (see above for why the Elemental Dragons breaking this is problematic in the extreme for reasons of cultural appropriation as well as the difficulty it causes for the overall narrative of Union as described in game). The fact that the Void Engineers are specifically described as having a significant Chinese component in their most recent incarnation. Trying to fathom how one can split hairs with Elemental Dragons vs. Technocratic Conventions in a mad mix &amp; match: All Elemental Dragon - Zaibatsu and nothing?, Elemental Dragon &amp; Union - Zaibatsu and the VE [but only if the launch is in China] &amp;the Syndicate and the VE [but only if the launch is NOT in China], or All Union - just the Syndicate and the VE's [as they are typically portrayed]. Etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}